  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Health Integration to Enhance Services in Eastern Uganda Activity (RHITES-E)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The RHITES-E Activity helps the government of Uganda expand access to and use of high-quality health services across 30 districts and two cities. The initiative reaches some 7 million people in Eastern Uganda and Karamoja with services for HIV/AIDS; malaria; tuberculosis; maternal, newborn and child health; family planning; WASH; and nutrition. Beginning in FY22, RHITES-E transitioned direct service delivery support to the MoH  at the district level, as well as strengthened several local recipients of direct USAID funding. In FY23, RHITES-E will further strengthen the governance, leadership and management capacity of 30 health districts, two regional referral hospitals and three local NGO/private Implementing Partners to increase accessibility, and utilization of quality integrated HIV, TB, and family health  services.  Major activities include addressing leadership and governance as well as staffing challenges at the district level. Through enhanced  multi-sectoral collaboration and planning, the program engages district and sub-county stakeholders to strengthen existing community structures, reduce drivers of teenage pregnancies, and promote adequate nutrition practices, among others. RHITES-E staff advise district health management teams and district mentors to carry out data-driven support supervision to improve the maternal and child health response, and to conduct health system strengthening (HSS) targeted to enhancing the overall district family health (FH) response. RHITES-E specialists facilitate meetings to review progress on the transition to local leadership and implementation of sustainability plans to improve quality and uptake of services in poorly performing health facilities. Though IntraHealths Data to Action (D2A) methodology, RHITES-E develops the capacity of health workers through technical working groups to review FH performance, identify service quality and access gaps, and plan follow up coaching and mentorship. RHITES-E strengthens qualit</narrative>
  </description>
